# =============================================================================
# syntax-refinement.sem  —  hello-world webserver, controlled-English revision
# =============================================================================
#
# Experimental dialect of SemanticScript. Not valid input to current ascc/semsc.
# Demonstrates the refined syntax in pure controlled English: no `=`, no `/`,
# no `@`, no `$`, no `%`, no `#`. The grammar carries kind; the lexeme carries
# name; the verb's slot tells you what each token is.
#
# Fifteen refinements, all anchored to one law:
#   "Every executable line is one English fact, anchored by subject,
#    and the verb names the role of every slot."
#
#   R1  One verb per slot                  (scopeOf / typeOf / mutabilityOf ...)
#   R2  Explicit bodyOf / endOperation     (no parser mode sniffing)
#   R3  English-named type constructors    (resultReturning ... failingWith)
#   R4  Parser-enforced call lifecycle     (call -> forParam* -> run -> bind)
#   R5  Atomic literals in value slots     (true, false, 8080, 5 seconds)
#   R6  Closed verb core, attribute lines  (each policy is a subject line)
#   R7  Policy lines anchored to the call  (timeoutOf / cancelOn / retryPolicyOf)
#   R8  Verb-grammar names the slot kind   (no sigils; rename walks the grammar)
#   R9  with ... endWith subject block     (subject re-emitted on retrieval)
#   R10 First-class atomic literals        (Bool, integer, duration, enum path)
#   R11 branchOn ... whenValue ... thenGoto (named decision primitive)
#   R12 Type echoed on every binding/param (every line is type-complete)
#   R13 Content-class literal prefixes     (plainText / urlPath / htmlBody / sqlBody)
#   R14 Line-leading provenance verbs      (frozen / proposed / generated)
#   R15 Lifecycle-aware ignore             (ignoreOkOf / ignoreErrorOf because ...)
#
# Identifier kinds (no sigils — the grammar and the lexeme convention carry it):
#   Types         PascalCase                       HttpRequest, HttpRoutePath
#   Dependencies  lowercase dot.path               http.requestMethodEquals
#   Operations    camelCase, action-style          handleRequest, main
#   Calls         camelCase, verb-phrase noun      methodCheck, buildOk
#   Values        camelCase, state-style noun      isGet, okResponse
#   Storage slots camelCase noun                   greetingBody, listenPort
#   Labels        camelCase with `at` prefix       atServeGreeting, atNotFound
#
# The kind of a slot is always the kind the verb requires there. A rename
# pass walks the grammar; it never grep-collides across kinds. A linter
# enforces the naming convention so a human skimming sees the kind too.
# =============================================================================


# R14: line-leading provenance verbs.
#   frozen     this line is review-frozen; agents need explicit unfreeze.
#   proposed   this line is an agent suggestion awaiting review.
#   generated  this line was produced by tooling; regenerate, do not edit.

frozen module app.hello_server
frozen purposeOf app.hello_server "Single-route HTTP hello-world demonstrating refined syntax."
frozen invariantOf app.hello_server "GET / and GET /healthz return 200 with a stable plaintext greeting; all other requests return 404."


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module storage (R1, R5, R10, R13)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each storage slot is one subject. Every axis is one verb anchored by that
# subject. Reordering the verbs is a no-op; slot-swap is ungrammatical because
# each axis has a verb whose argument kind it alone accepts.

storage greetingBody
scopeOf greetingBody module
mutabilityOf greetingBody immutable
typeOf greetingBody PlainTextBody
initialValueOf greetingBody plainText "Hello, world!\n"

storage notFoundBody
scopeOf notFoundBody module
mutabilityOf notFoundBody immutable
typeOf notFoundBody PlainTextBody
initialValueOf notFoundBody plainText "Not found\n"

storage listenPort
scopeOf listenPort module
mutabilityOf listenPort immutable
typeOf listenPort TcpPort
initialValueOf listenPort 8080

storage rootPath
scopeOf rootPath module
mutabilityOf rootPath immutable
typeOf rootPath HttpRoutePath
initialValueOf rootPath urlPath "/"

storage healthPath
scopeOf healthPath module
mutabilityOf healthPath immutable
typeOf healthPath HttpRoutePath
initialValueOf healthPath urlPath "/healthz"

storage bootTimeout
scopeOf bootTimeout module
mutabilityOf bootTimeout immutable
typeOf bootTimeout Duration
initialValueOf bootTimeout 5 seconds

storage stopTimeout
scopeOf stopTimeout module
mutabilityOf stopTimeout immutable
typeOf stopTimeout Duration
initialValueOf stopTimeout 10 seconds


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Type aliases (R3)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generic type constructors get English names that bake arity into the verb.
# `resultReturning X failingWith Y` is binary by grammar. `mapOf K toType V`
# is binary by grammar. The reader never needs to know constructor arity.

typeAlias RequestHandleResult resultReturning HttpResponse failingWith HandlerError
typeAlias StartServerResult   resultReturning ServerHandle failingWith StartError
typeAlias StopServerResult    resultReturning StopStatus   failingWith StopError


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

importDependency standard.http     aliasedTo http
importDependency standard.log      aliasedTo log
importDependency standard.runtime  aliasedTo runtime


# =============================================================================
# operation handleRequest
# =============================================================================
# R2: `operation NAME` opens the contract zone; `bodyOf NAME` opens the body
# zone; `endOperation NAME` closes it. No mode sniffing. Every contract line
# names the operation as its subject.
# =============================================================================

operation handleRequest
inputOf handleRequest httpRequest asType HttpRequest
inputOf handleRequest httpSession asType HttpSession
outputOf handleRequest asType RequestHandleResult
readsResource handleRequest http.request
writesResource handleRequest http.response
authorityOf handleRequest overResource http.response permittingAction write
memoryPolicyOf handleRequest usingArena scopedTo request budgetedAt 8 kibibytes
asyncOf handleRequest no
mayFailWith handleRequest HandlerError
purposeOf handleRequest "Route one inbound HTTP request: GET / and GET /healthz return the greeting; all other requests return 404."
invariantOf handleRequest "No request data is logged or persisted; bodies are constant module storage."

bodyOf handleRequest

  # R4: parser-enforced lifecycle. For each call name, the grammar requires
  #     call -> (policy lines)* -> forParam* -> run -> bind*
  # Out-of-order lines are a parse error. The verb at the start of every
  # line names the lifecycle position; the call name names the subject.
  #
  # R12: every forParam carries the parameter's declared type, so a line
  # retrieved in isolation is type-complete without consulting the callee.

  call methodCheck targeting http.requestMethodEquals
  forParam methodCheck request asType HttpRequest passing httpRequest
  forParam methodCheck method  asType HttpMethod  passing HttpMethod.Get
  run methodCheck
  bindResultOf methodCheck named isGet asType Bool

  call pathCheckRoot targeting http.requestPathEquals
  forParam pathCheckRoot request asType HttpRequest   passing httpRequest
  forParam pathCheckRoot path    asType HttpRoutePath passing rootPath
  run pathCheckRoot
  bindResultOf pathCheckRoot named isRoot asType Bool

  call pathCheckHealth targeting http.requestPathEquals
  forParam pathCheckHealth request asType HttpRequest   passing httpRequest
  forParam pathCheckHealth path    asType HttpRoutePath passing healthPath
  run pathCheckHealth
  bindResultOf pathCheckHealth named isHealth asType Bool

  call anyKnownPath targeting logic.or
  forParam anyKnownPath left  asType Bool passing isRoot
  forParam anyKnownPath right asType Bool passing isHealth
  run anyKnownPath
  bindResultOf anyKnownPath named isKnownPath asType Bool

  # R11: structured-flow primitive. `branchOn` opens one named decision;
  # each `whenValue` is one outcome record; `endBranch` closes it. A
  # retrieved `whenValue` line still names the discriminant and the
  # destination (tooling re-emits the `branchOn` subject on retrieval).
  branchOn isGet asType Bool
    whenValue true  thenGoto atCheckPath
    whenValue false thenGoto atNotFound
  endBranch

  label atCheckPath
  branchOn isKnownPath asType Bool
    whenValue true  thenGoto atServeGreeting
    whenValue false thenGoto atNotFound
  endBranch

  label atServeGreeting
  call buildOk targeting http.responsePlainText
  forParam buildOk status asType HttpStatus    passing HttpStatus.Ok
  forParam buildOk body   asType PlainTextBody passing greetingBody
  run buildOk
  bindResultOf buildOk named okResponse asType HttpResponse
  returnOkOf handleRequest withValue okResponse asType HttpResponse

  label atNotFound
  call build404 targeting http.responsePlainText
  forParam build404 status asType HttpStatus    passing HttpStatus.NotFound
  forParam build404 body   asType PlainTextBody passing notFoundBody
  run build404
  bindResultOf build404 named notFoundResponse asType HttpResponse
  returnOkOf handleRequest withValue notFoundResponse asType HttpResponse

endOperation handleRequest


# =============================================================================
# operation main
# =============================================================================

operation main
outputOf main asType ExitCode
allocatesResource main net.tcpListener
bindsResource main net.tcpPort
spawnsResource main runtime.taskGroup
readsResource main os.signal
authorityOf main overResource net.tcpListener permittingAction allocate
authorityOf main overResource net.tcpPort     permittingAction bind
authorityOf main overResource os.signal       permittingAction read
memoryPolicyOf main usingHeap budgetedAt 64 kibibytes
asyncOf main no
purposeOf main "Bind one HTTP listener on the configured port and dispatch requests to handleRequest until an OS shutdown signal arrives."
invariantOf main "Listener lifetime is bounded by the enclosing task group; shutdown is structured and produces a typed StopStatus."

bodyOf main

  # R7: policy lines are anchored to the call name, between `call` and the
  # first `forParam`. Each policy is one fact on one line — `timeoutOf`,
  # `cancelOn`, `retryPolicyOf` — and each names its subject.
  call bootServer targeting http.serverStart
  timeoutOf bootServer passing bootTimeout
  cancelOn bootServer passing processShutdownToken
  retryPolicyOf bootServer none
  forParam bootServer port    asType TcpPort          passing listenPort
  forParam bootServer handler asType HttpHandler      passing handleRequest
  forParam bootServer logger  asType StructuredLogger passing log.default
  run bootServer
  bindOkOf    bootServer named serverHandle asType ServerHandle
  bindErrorOf bootServer named startError   asType StartError
  branchOnErrorOf bootServer thenGoto atStartFailed

  # R9: `with SUBJECT ... endWith` block. The subject is named once at
  # block open. Inside the block, `forParam` / `run` / `bindResultOf`
  # drop the subject slot; tooling re-emits it when surfacing any single
  # contained line to an agent. The block is delimited by the explicit
  # `endWith` token, so indentation is cosmetic.
  with awaitShutdown targeting runtime.awaitAnySignal
    forParam signal asType OsSignal passing OsSignal.Interrupt
    forParam signal asType OsSignal passing OsSignal.Terminate
    run
    bindResultOf named shutdownReason asType ShutdownReason
  endWith

  call stopServer targeting http.serverStop
  timeoutOf stopServer passing stopTimeout
  forParam stopServer server asType ServerHandle   passing serverHandle
  forParam stopServer reason asType ShutdownReason passing shutdownReason
  run stopServer
  bindOkOf    stopServer named stopStatus asType StopStatus
  bindErrorOf stopServer named stopError  asType StopError
  # R15: lifecycle-aware ignore with mandatory rationale. The verb names
  # which arm is discarded; `because "..."` is required. A bare ignore on
  # a Result whose error arm has not been handled is a linter error.
  ignoreErrorOf stopServer because "Process is exiting; a failed graceful stop is logged elsewhere and does not change the exit code."

  call logStop targeting log.info
  forParam logStop event  asType LogEventKind passing LogEventKind.ServerStopped
  forParam logStop status asType StopStatus   passing stopStatus
  run logStop
  ignoreOkOf logStop because "Logging is best-effort and never fails the request path."

  returnValueOf main withValue ExitCode.Ok asType ExitCode

  label atStartFailed
  call logFailure targeting log.error
  forParam logFailure event  asType LogEventKind passing LogEventKind.StartupFailed
  forParam logFailure detail asType StartError   passing startError
  run logFailure
  ignoreOkOf logFailure because "Logging is best-effort and never fails startup-failure reporting."
  returnValueOf main withValue ExitCode.StartupFailed asType ExitCode

endOperation main


# =============================================================================
# Generated route registry — regenerate, do not hand-edit. (R14)
# =============================================================================

generated route forMethod HttpMethod.Get atPath rootPath   dispatchedTo handleRequest
generated route forMethod HttpMethod.Get atPath healthPath dispatchedTo handleRequest


# =============================================================================
# Notes on what changed and why
# =============================================================================
#
# Why no sigils (R8 revised):
#   Sigils (@call, $value, %slot, #label) were imported from shell and config
#   languages. They are foreign punctuation, exactly the kind the language
#   forbids elsewhere. The job sigils were doing — telling a reader which
#   namespace a token lives in — is done better by two things working
#   together:
#     1. The verb that uses the token. `call NAME targeting TARGET` declares
#        NAME as a call. `bindResultOf CALL named VALUE asType T` references
#        CALL and declares VALUE. The verb's grammar locks each slot's kind.
#     2. A naming convention enforced by the linter. Calls are verb-phrase
#        nouns. Values are state nouns. Labels carry an `at` prefix in the
#        lexeme itself, so `atStartFailed` reads as a label without a sigil.
#   A rename pass walks the grammar, not the lexeme — so renames are
#   kind-aware automatically and homonyms across kinds do not collide.
#
# Why per-slot verbs (R1) instead of `key=value`:
#   `=` is config-file punctuation, not English. `scopeOf X module` reads
#   as a fact; `scope=module` reads as a config entry. The parser cost is
#   identical; the agent-prior cost is not.
#
# Why English-named type constructors (R3) instead of `Result/2`:
#   `/` is foreign punctuation; arity numerals are a parser hint, not a
#   semantic carrier. `resultReturning X failingWith Y` carries the same
#   arity *and* names what each slot is for.
#
# Why subject-anchored attribute lines (R6, R7) instead of one fused line:
#   Fusing `timeout`/`cancelOn`/`retry` onto the `call` line traded line
#   count for slot density and reintroduced positional ambiguity. Each
#   policy on its own line, anchored by call name, keeps every line a
#   single retrievable fact.
#
# Why line-leading provenance verbs (R14) instead of `*` / `~` / `+`:
#   Punctuation prefixes don't carry meaning in their shape and are easy
#   to drop on partial retrieval. `frozen module app.hello_server` reads
#   as a fact and participates in lint as a normal token.
#
# What is intentionally unchanged from the current dialect:
#   - Verb-first lines, controlled English vocabulary.
#   - camelCase identifiers, PascalCase types, dot.path dependency paths.
#   - Named call objects, named labels, declared effects / authorities /
#     memory / async / failure / purpose / invariant.
#   - Typed comments (rationale, invariant, warning, agent, memory, ...).
#   - "Every line is one semantic fact" and "repetition preserves context."
